Unbound Wrath Edition — allow talent learning for unlocked classes

Found on the VM 2026-08-15, during the first real `wow update` run. This hunk
is NOT part of the shipped `unbound-core-access.patch`: `Player::LearnTalent`
has xinef's anti-cheat gate rejecting any talent whose tab does not match the
character's class mask, so a multiclass character could unlock a class through
the Mentor, learn its spells, and still be refused its talents.

Recorded here because it was undocumented local work living only in the VM's
working tree. `wow update` carries it across on git's stash like any other
local edit (the shipped Unbound patch is reverted and re-applied separately),
but an edit that exists in exactly one place, uncommitted, on one machine, is
one `git checkout --` away from gone.

Sibling of `2026-08-15-feral-spirit-coexist.patch`, same reasoning.

NB this hunk is why the first `wow update` refused the core: the post-revert
check asked "is `UnboundClassMask` gone from all six files?", and this second,
independent reference kept answering no even though the revert had worked
perfectly. The check now asks whether the shipped patch itself can re-apply,
which is the question that was always meant.

diff --git a/src/server/game/Entities/Player/Player.cpp b/src/server/game/Entities/Player/Player.cpp
--- a/src/server/game/Entities/Player/Player.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Entities/Player/Player.cpp
@@ -14293,7 +14295,7 @@ void Player::LearnTalent(uint32 talentId, uint32 talentRank, bool command /*= fa

     // xinef: prevent learn talent for different class (cheating)
-    if ((getClassMask() & talentTabInfo->ClassMask) == 0)
+    if (((getClassMask() | GetUnboundClassMask()) & talentTabInfo->ClassMask) == 0)
         return;

     // xinef: find current talent rank
